    {
      "section": "hero.center",
      "variant": "square",
      "content": {
        "title": "Numbers auditors can trace end to end.",
        "lead": "Banks, insurers and fintechs answer to examiners for every figure. Lattice records how each number was built, tested and approved, one click away.",
        "primary": {
          "label": "Book a session with our finance data team",
          "href": "/contact"
        },
        "media": {
          "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
          "alt": "Ledger transactions flowing into balance and settlement models",
          "ref": "/assets/pages/hero/financial-services.svg"
        }
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "stroke.draw-on",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "render-final-state"
      },
      "style": {
        "strokeShape": "stroke.s4",
        "strokeGradient": "gradient.01"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "features.card-grid",
      "variant": "four-column",
      "content": {
        "eyebrow": "Built for banking and insurance",
        "title": "Where finance teams use Lattice",
        "body": "From quarterly filings to fraud models, firms that move money need numbers that are right the first time and explainable years later. Here is where banks, insurers and payment firms use Lattice to keep reports accurate and products shipping.",
        "cards": [
          {
            "icon": {
              "assetRole": "icon.feature",
              "alt": "",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/icons/clipboard.svg"
            },
            "title": "Examination-ready reporting pipelines",
            "body": "Every change to a capital, liquidity or risk model is a reviewed pull request with a named approver and a timestamp. When an examiner asks how a figure came to be, you simply share the lineage graph and the commit log."
          },
          {
            "icon": {
              "assetRole": "icon.feature",
              "alt": "",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/icons/dollar.svg"
            },
            "title": "One ledger, one answer",
            "body": "Finance, risk and treasury stop reconciling three versions of net interest margin. Shared metric logic lives in one tested project, so the close is quicker, variance meetings are shorter and restatements rare."
          },
          {
            "icon": {
              "assetRole": "icon.feature",
              "alt": "",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/icons/shield.svg"
            },
            "title": "Lock down account and payment records",
            "body": "Mask card numbers and personal details by role, encrypt data in transit and at rest, and log each query against sensitive tables. Analysts get what their job requires and nothing more, which keeps auditors calm."
          },
          {
            "icon": {
              "assetRole": "icon.feature",
              "alt": "",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/icons/chart.svg"
            },
            "title": "Keep up with trading-day volumes",
            "body": "Tick data, card swipes and claims arrive by the billion. Incremental models process only new records, parallel runs finish before markets open, and separate projects let each line of business scale its own pipelines."
          }
        ]
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "iconSize": "size.icon.32",
        "headerAlign": "start",
        "paddingTop": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "social-proof.quote-band",
