        "quotes": [
          {
            "logo": {
              "assetRole": "customer.logo",
              "alt": "Halcyon",
              "ref": "/assets/marquee/logo-6.svg"
            },
            "quote": "Our last exam closed without a single finding. Examiners saw lineage and approvals behind every number and finished early.",
            "person": "Grace Okafor",
            "role": "Chief Data Officer"
          }
        ]
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "static",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "none-needed"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "features.card-grid",
      "variant": "wash-icon",
      "content": {
        "title": "Opening up new data use cases",
        "body": "Once reporting is under control, the same trusted models can power growth work in lending, risk and customer service.",
        "cards": [
          {
            "icon": {
              "assetRole": "icon.feature",
              "alt": "",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/icons/rocket.svg"
            },
            "title": "Faster product launches",
            "body": "Stand up the data behind a new card, loan or savings product in weeks by reusing tested customer and account models already in production."
          },
          {
            "icon": {
              "assetRole": "icon.feature",
              "alt": "",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/icons/user.svg"
            },
            "title": "Every account holder in one profile",
            "body": "Link checking, mortgage, card and investment records into one household view, so pricing, credit limits and retention offers reflect the full relationship with each customer and adjust automatically as their circumstances shift."
          },
          {
            "icon": {
              "assetRole": "icon.feature",
              "alt": "",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/icons/sparkle.svg"
            },
            "title": "Models your risk team can sign off",
            "body": "Feed credit scoring and fraud detection with documented, versioned training data, so model risk teams can approve faster and explain every input."
          }
        ]
      },
      "motion": {
        "pattern": "reveal.fade-up",
        "reducedMotionFallback": "show-immediately"
      },
      "style": {
        "iconSize": "size.icon.32",
        "headerAlign": "center",
        "paddingTop": "none"
      }
    },
    {
      "section": "features.tabs-dark",
      "variant": "default",
      "content": {
        "title": "Move at fintech speed while keeping every control a modern bank requires",
        "body": "Lattice gives finance data teams one reviewed workflow for every model, so controls hold up in audits, policies apply the same way everywhere and more people across the bank can use data safely.",
        "tabs": [
          {
            "title": "Reviewed SQL models with a sign-off on every change",
            "body": "Each model is plain SQL kept in Git, so every edit has a diff, a reviewer and a rollback path. Docs are generated as you build and tests run on every merge, letting teams ship every week and still satisfy model risk and audit.",
            "media": {
              "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
              "alt": "Column-level lineage from raw orders to a revenue model",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/tabs/dark-4.svg"
            }
          },
          {
            "title": "Trace every figure back to its source",
            "body": "Click any number in a regulatory return and walk upstream through each join and filter to the raw feed, next to the commits, reviews and approvals that shaped it.",
            "media": {
              "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
              "alt": "Column-level lineage from raw orders to a revenue model",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/tabs/dark-4.svg"
            }
          },
          {
            "title": "Separation of duties, enforced by design",
            "body": "Developers build against masked copies in their own environments, production runs under service accounts, and SSO plus role policies decide who sees raw account data.",
            "media": {
              "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
              "alt": "Catalog search results with owners and certification",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/tabs/dark-8.svg"
            }
          },
          {
            "title": "Compliance and finance sign off on a single shared change",
            "body": "Controllers and compliance officers read plain-language docs, comment on edits and approve them where engineers work, so sign-off is never an email chain.",
            "media": {
              "assetRole": "product.screenshot",
              "alt": "Editor suggesting a uniqueness test while a model is written",
              "ref": "/assets/pages/tabs/dark-2.svg"
            }
          },
          {
            "title": "Grow lines of business safely",
            "body": "Retail, commercial and wealth units each own a project and share core models through versioned contracts, so one team’s edit never breaks another.",
            "media": {
